<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SharingRules xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        RULE 4, Lead_Acquisition_Team_All, ADDED 2026-08-17. "Every Lead must be visible to
        the acquisition team" (explicit business requirement) was NOT satisfied by rules 1-3
        above, confirmed by measurement, not assumption:

          - Rule 1 (Lead_Acquisition_Queue_RW) shares Leads OWNED BY THE Acquisition QUEUE.
            Live Lead ownership in this org has ZERO rows owned by that queue (queried
            2026-08-17: 41 owned by the System Administrator user, 1 owned by Junior Dhanani
            himself) - LeadConvertService/EmailToLeadService never assign the queue as owner.
          - Rules 2 and 3 (Lead_Acquisition_Broker / Lead_IR_Investor) are RecordTypeId
            criteria rules. 41 of the 42 live Leads have RecordTypeId = null (no record type
            assigned), so neither rule's `equals` criterion ever matches them.
          - UserRecordAccess was queried directly for both Junior Dhanani and Nikhil Dhanani
            against several admin-owned, null-record-type Leads: HasReadAccess=false,
            HasEditAccess=false, MaxAccessLevel=None for both users on every one of them,
            confirming zero effective Lead sharing exists today regardless of what is
            committed in this file.

        WHY A NEW CRITERIA RULE, NOT AN OWNER RULE ON THE SYSTEM ADMINISTRATOR ROLE. The
        System Administrator user who owns 41/42 Leads has NO UserRole assigned (confirmed by
        query) - a Role-based sharedFrom can never reach an owner with no Role, and any other
        future owner (another admin, an Automated Process running the Broker Protection
        pipeline) is equally unpredictable. A criteria-based rule shares by what the RECORD
        IS, never by who owns it, so it is the only construct that can guarantee "every Lead"
        rather than "every Lead owned by a role we happened to enumerate."

        WHY Company != '' AS THE CRITERION. Salesforce criteria rules require at least one
        criteriaItem; there is no literal "match everything" option. Company is a required
        standard Lead field - and this org's own EmailToLeadService.COMPANY_PLACEHOLDER
        convention (ARCHITECTURE.md) confirms it is never left blank even on
        automation-created Leads - so "Company notEqual blank" is true for every Lead that has
        ever existed or ever will. This has NO precedent elsewhere in this repo's
        sharingRules/ folder (verified by grep before writing it) - the LOI__c file's own
        comment records the same situation for its RecordTypeId value format ("the one
        element below with no in-repo precedent"). 🔴 CreatedDate WAS TRIED FIRST AND
        REJECTED AT DEPLOY: "Custom Field Definition ID: bad value for restricted picklist
        field: CreatedDate" - audit/system fields are apparently not eligible
        SharingCriteriaRule criteria fields on this object, confirmed by measurement, not
        assumed. Company was substituted and deployed clean. If a future edit ever needs a
        different always-true field, expect the same restriction and confirm at deploy first.

        WHY DPEG_Acquisitions_Team AND NOT A SECOND Principals RULE (unlike the NDA__c /
        LOI__c disposition pattern, which needs two rules for two populations). Queried
        directly: DPEG_Acquisitions_Team's only two members are the Role group for "DPEG
        Principal" and the RoleAndSubordinatesInternal group for "Acquisitions Analyst" - i.e.
        Nikhil Dhanani (DPEG Principal role) and Junior Dhanani (Acquisitions Analyst role,
        a child of DPEG Principal) are BOTH already inside this one group by role nesting.
        A second rule to a Principals group would be redundant here, unlike the disposition
        objects where Principals sit outside DPEG_Acquisitions_Team's membership.

        ACCESS LEVEL IS Edit, AND OBJECT CRUD IS STILL THE CEILING - matching the pattern used
        throughout this repo's other sharing rules. DPEG_Acquisition_Edit (Junior's set) grants
        allowEdit=true on Lead; DPEG_Acquisition_View (Nikhil's, via DPEG_Principal_PSG) grants
        allowRead=true / allowEdit=false. Sharing this rule at Edit does not over-grant Nikhil -
        his own object CRUD still caps him to Read.

        🔴 DEPLOY ONE RULE AT A TIME - established in the 2026-07-22 RBAC build and repeated by
        every sharing-rule file added since (see NDA__c.sharingRules-meta.xml,
        LOI__c.sharingRules-meta.xml). Rules 1-3 in this file were committed on 2026-07-22 but
        are, per the measurement above, NOT currently live in this org - deploy this file in
        two passes: first rules 1-3 exactly as they already exist, confirming that state
        independently; then this rule 4 alone, so a rejection of the untested CreatedDate
        criterion cannot roll back rules 1-3 with it.

        🔴 GROUP MEMBERSHIP IS NOT DEPLOYABLE METADATA and CRITERIA-BASED SHARING RECALCULATES
        ASYNCHRONOUSLY - both standing cautions from the LOI__c/NDA__c files apply identically
        here. Verify post-deploy via UserRecordAccess for both Junior and Nikhil against a
        broad sample of Leads, not just the record(s) used to author this rule.
    -->
    <sharingOwnerRules>
        <fullName>Lead_Acquisition_Queue_RW</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <label>Lead Acquisition Queue RW</label>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Acquisitions_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
        <sharedFrom>
            <queue>Acquisition</queue>
        </sharedFrom>
    </sharingOwnerRules>
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>Lead_Acquisition_Broker</fullName>
        <label>Lead Acquisition Broker</label>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>RecordTypeId</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Acquisition Broker</value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Acquisitions_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>Lead_IR_Investor</fullName>
        <label>Lead IR Investor</label>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>RecordTypeId</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>IR Investor</value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>Investor_Relations</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>Lead_Acquisition_Team_All</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <description>Business requirement: every Lead must be visible to the acquisition team, regardless of owner or record type. Company is used as an always-true criterion (standard Lead.Company is required and this org's own EmailToLeadService.COMPANY_PLACEHOLDER convention confirms it is never left blank, even on automation-created Leads) because owner/role-based sharing cannot reach an owner with no Role (the System Administrator user who owns 41/42 live Leads), and 41 of those 42 have RecordTypeId null so rules 2/3 above never match them either. CreatedDate was tried first and rejected by the org at deploy time ("bad value for restricted picklist field: CreatedDate") - audit/system fields are not eligible SharingCriteriaRule criteria fields here, so a real, always-populated business field was substituted. See the in-root comment at the top of this file for the full measurement.</description>
        <label>Lead Acquisition Team All</label>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Company</field>
            <operation>notEqual</operation>
            <value></value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Acquisitions_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
</SharingRules>

